<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    v0.67.0: Tamil translations of the new v0.66.x
    journal chrome. Tamil is one of the three Indian
    languages the v0.67.0 D-6 localisation pass adds
    (Tamil / Hindi / Kannada). Crisis line NUMBERS
    stay in code (JournalToday.kt) — they are the
    public-safety digits and must be exact. The
    NAMES (iCall / Vandrevala / AASRA / Tele-MANAS)
    are kept verbatim because they are brand names
    of the operating helplines; translating them
    would lose the connection to the actual service.
    The hours-of-availability lines and the rest of
    the chrome are translated.

    The strings here mirror the keys in
    res/values/strings.xml. Only the v0.67.0 keys are
    listed — the rest of the v0.66.x strings fall
    back to the English default if a user is in the
    Tamil locale but reads an older surface.
-->
